WEBVTT

00:25:59.345 --> 00:26:02.140
the only system that we know
is inhabited, right,

00:26:02.181 --> 00:26:04.350
is our solar system.
ND: Right.

00:26:04.350 --> 00:26:08.229
HH: Is it required that you have
giant planets in the outer system

00:26:08.229 --> 00:26:10.398
and small planets
in the inner solar system

00:26:10.398 --> 00:26:12.066
to make habitability?

00:26:12.066 --> 00:26:14.485
Or is it just by happenstance?

00:26:14.485 --> 00:26:17.947
Did you have to have a Jupiter
to make it habitable?

00:26:17.947 --> 00:26:23.286
Did you have to have a Neptune
to sweep out through the Kuiper Belt

00:26:23.328 --> 00:26:25.830
and deliver volatiles
to the inner solar system,

00:26:25.872 --> 00:26:27.415
water and stuff?

00:26:27.457 --> 00:26:30.627
I mean, that's so interesting. And ...